            <ArticleTitle>Perspectives on irritable bowel syndrome: where have we been? Where are we now?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1586/17474124.2013.820050</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Irritable bowel syndrome is a chronic functional disorder with a complex etiology and multiple overlapping symptoms. Irritable bowel syndrome is characterized by long-lasting abdominal pain or discomfort, abnormal bowel habits and typically inadequate response to many of the available therapies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
